{"id": "EUVD-2026-85236", "enisaUuid": "4fe1eb84-89ac-3050-a6e2-7d438e82cdd2", "description": "Improper handling of length parameter inconsistency vulnerability in Apache Tomcat allows WebSocket message smuggling when per-message-deflate is used.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Tomcat: from 11.0.0-M1 through 11.0.25, from 10.1.0-M1 through 10.1.59, from 9.0.0.M1 through 9.0.121.\n\n\n\nThe following versions were EOS at the time the CVE was created but are known to be affected:\u00a0from 8.5.0 through 8.5.100, from 7.0.56 through 7.0.109.\u00a0Other unsupported versions may also be affected.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 11.0.26, 10.1.60 or 9.1.22, which fix the issue.", "datePublished": "2026-09-23T11:32:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-23T18:10:52", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://lists.apache.org/thread/ypvlkjqsq0480fnk9jm6h9qllddwlw4w"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-87022", "GHSA-xwrc-v28h-528j"], "assigner": "apache", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4925738b-60ad-3939-bd57-e4a885167107", "product": {"name": "Apache Tomcat", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "9.0.0.M1 \u22649.0.121"}, {"id": "8f45a6ea-55cb-388b-8a88-5a4fa3d23a7e", "product": {"name": "Apache Tomcat", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "8.5.0 \u22648.5.100"}, {"id": "b984dc72-8e45-39da-a803-2ea083f01660", "product": {"name": "Apache Tomcat", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "7.0.56 \u22647.0.109"}, {"id": "d4da9144-6dc5-3998-9b66-a51e7a40548c", "product": {"name": "Apache Tomcat", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "10.1.0-M1 \u226410.1.59"}, {"id": "eb20d99f-1518-337a-8513-605e34e2a723", "product": {"name": "Apache Tomcat", "vendor": {"name": "Apache Software Foundation"}}, "product_version": "11.0.0-M1 \u226411.0.25"}], "enisaIdVend